  "lineage": "Luanda's urban Angolan dance music codified in the musseques between the late 1950s and 1975 by Bonga, Ngola Ritmos, Os Kiezos and David Zé — 100-120 BPM in a two-feel with a snapping snare-and-rim accent, dikanza scraper and interlocking nylon-and-electric guitar counterpoint under raspy Kimbundu lead vocals whose lyrics carried nationalist and street commentary.",
